    <!-- how it works -->
    <string name="how_title">How Voxara works</string>
    <string name="how_measure_title">What is measured</string>
    <string name="how_measure_body">The watch\'s microphone takes short readings of the sound level around you. It keeps only the numbers (decibels). Audio is never recorded, stored or sent.</string>
    <string name="how_aweight_title">A-weighting</string>
    <string name="how_aweight_body">Levels are A-weighted (dBA), like the ear hears: very low and very high frequencies count less.</string>
    <string name="how_sustained_title">Sustained, not instant</string>
    <string name="how_sustained_body">Level alerts use a 3-minute average, so a single bang never triggers one.</string>
    <string name="how_niosh_title">Daily dose (NIOSH)</string>
    <string name="how_niosh_body" formatted="false">85 dBA for 8 hours is 100% of the day. Every 3 dB more halves the time: 88 dBA for 4 hours, 94 dBA for 1 hour.</string>
    <string name="how_who_title">Weekly budget (WHO)</string>
    <string name="how_who_body">The 7-day budget follows WHO-ITU H.870: 80 dB for 40 hours a week (75 dB for sensitive listeners). It rolls: old exposure drops off day by day.</string>
    <string name="how_headphones_title">Headphones</string>
    <string name="how_headphones_body">Headphone levels are estimated from the volume and the type of output (±10 dB); the microphone never listens to them. Each minute counts once: headphones or surroundings, whichever is louder at the ear.</string>
    <string name="how_accuracy_title">Accuracy</string>
    <string name="how_accuracy_body">Watch microphones are not sound level meters: expect ±3–5 dB after calibration, more without. Treat every number as an estimate.</string>
    <string name="how_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="how_privacy_body">Only numbers are stored, and they travel only between your own watch and phone. Cloud AI is optional and off by default; it sees rounded totals only.</string>
    <string name="how_medical_title">Not a medical device</string>
    <string name="how_medical_body">Voxara helps with listening habits. It does not diagnose or treat. If you notice ringing, muffled hearing or ear pain, see a hearing professional.</string>

